## Trust, safety & buying advice

Gumtree is committed to safeguarding its community against online harms. The platform takes a three-pillar approach to safety: promoting positive behaviour, deterring bad actors, and striving to be best in class.

### Safety advice for buyers

- Be wary of deals that seem too good to be true
- Never send money via bank transfer, Western Union, or MoneyGram to someone you haven't met
- Use cash whenever possible and inspect the item before paying
- Meet in a public place for transactions when possible
- Be suspicious of sellers located overseas or who make excuses for not meeting in person
- For mobile phones, check the IMEI number to ensure it hasn't been reported lost or stolen
- For vehicles, verify documentation, check the V5 logbook, and consider an HPI check
- When buying from a private seller, the principle of "caveat emptor" (buyer beware) applies

### Safety advice for sellers

- Be cautious of buyers who offer to pay more than the asking price
- Be wary of requests to ship items before payment clears
- Meet in a safe, public location when possible
- Don't share personal or financial information unnecessarily

### Reporting

- Users can report suspicious listings or users via the "Report" button on any listing or profile
- Suspected fraud can also be reported to Action Fraud (UK's national reporting centre for fraud and cybercrime)

### Key safety links

- Help centre: https://help.gumtree.com
